<title>AUSTRALIA: Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Aug 19.</title>
<headline>Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Aug 19.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Monday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name			 P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Mayne Nickless	   407.92   8.24</p>
<p> 2   Ranger Minerals	  182.69   3.80</p>
<p> 3   Syd Hrbr Casino	  159.92   1.94</p>
<p> 4   Perilya Mines	    129.27   0.53</p>
<p> 5   Energy Equity	    114.84   1.47</p>
<p> 6   Central Norseman	 104.17   0.50</p>
<p> 7   Tap Oil		     94.89   1.67</p>
<p> 8   Consol Paper		80.88   2.75</p>
<p> 9   Bougainville		78.13   0.50</p>
<p>10   Computershare	     75.18  13.30</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Climax Mining		1.45   0.72</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile		3.12   0.70</p>
<p> 3   Haoma Mining		 5.06   0.25</p>
<p> 4   Holyman			5.11   1.75</p>
<p> 5   Renison Goldflds	   5.28   3.60</p>
<p> 6   Jardine Fm China	   5.87   0.87</p>
<p> 7   Emperor Mines		6.87   0.99</p>
<p> 8   Gwalia Consol		6.99   1.35</p>
<p> 9   Mt Leyshon Gold	    7.10   1.65</p>
<p>10   Premier Inv		  7.18   1.69</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
